\f0\fs24 \cf0 <div class="tei-head wp-block-heading has-text-align-center">Incipit</div>\
\
<div class="tei-poem-static middle-english">\
    <h4 class="tei-head-column">Middle English</h3>\
\
    <!-- Stanza 1 -->\
    <div class="tei-line">First myn vnkunnynge and my rudenesse</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">Vnto yow alle that lysten knowe her chaunce</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">By caste of dyse in your hertys impresse</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">And by[efn_note]MS Bodl. 638 <i>my</i>, MS Fairfax 16 <i>by</i>.[/efn_note] goode wille to doon folkes plesaunce</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">Alle be I haue of wytte no suffisaunce</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">This worldes course I haue herd sey ful ryve</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">Ys that alle folke shall not at ones thryve.</div>\
    \
    <span class="tei-stanza-break"></span>\
    \
    <!-- Stanza 2 -->\
    <div class="tei-line">I pray to god that euery wight may caste</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">Vpon three dyse ryght as is in hys herte</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">Whether he be rechelesse or stedfaste</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">So moote he [su_permalink id="https://quod.lib.umich.edu/m/middle-english-dictionary/dictionary/MED24826/track?counter=1&search_id=5005138" target="blank" title="lawghen" rel="definition"]lawghen[/su_permalink] outher elles smerte</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">He that is gilty his lyfe to converte</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">They that in trouthe haue suffred many a throwe</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">Moote ther chaunce fal as they moote be knowe</div>\
    \
    <span class="tei-stanza-break"></span>\
    \
    <!-- Stanza 3 -->\
    <div class="tei-line">Syth fortune hathe of alle thynge gouernaunce</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">How euer ye happe excused holdeth me</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">ffor neyther am I worthy to bere penaunce</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">Ne thanke truly in no maner degre</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">But natheles this wol I sey for me</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">She that yow beste may helpen in this nede</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">Ryght wel to caste I pre(y) fortune yow spede</div>\
</div>\
\
<div class="tei-poem-static modern-english">\
    <h4 class="tei-head-column">Modern English</h3>\
\
    <!-- Stanza 1 -->\
    <div class="tei-line">First my ignorance and my uncouthness</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">unto all of you who want to know your fate</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">By cast of dice impress on your hearts</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">And by good will to satisfy others</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">Even though I don\'92t really know</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">The ways of the world I\'92ve heard it said</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">That not everyone can thrive at once</div>\
    \
    <span class="tei-stanza-break"></span>\
    \
    <!-- Stanza 2 -->\
    <div class="tei-line">I pray to God that every person may cast</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">Upon three dice Just what is in his heart</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">Whether he is reckless or steadfast</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">That He might scorn or else harm</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">He who is guilty To change his life</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">Those who in truth have suffered many such rolls</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">Might their fortune fall so they might learn</div>\
    \
    <span class="tei-stanza-break"></span>\
    \
    <!-- Stanza 3 -->\
    <div class="tei-line">Since fortune governs all things</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">Whatever happens, pardon me</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">For I am not worthy to bear responsibility</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">Or thanks, really, to any degree</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">But nevertheless, I\'92ll say this for myself</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">She who can best help you in this need</div>\
    <div class="tei-line">To roll right well I pray Fortune speeds you</div>\
</div>}